# The Gradle wrapper is TRACKED, deliberately (product-audit run 2, F2). These
# three files were ignored by the Flutter scaffold, so `git archive HEAD` produced
# an android/ with no `gradlew` — and the gate's `kotlin compile` lane, added
# precisely because GREEN had never been evidence about KeystoreVault.kt or
# RevealActivity.kt, therefore could not run in CI at all. It did not go RED; it
# emitted no row, and strict mode counts SKIPs, not absences.
#
# All three, not just the two the Linux lane needs: `gradle wrapper` regenerates
# them as one artifact, so a tracked gradlew beside an ignored gradlew.bat
# desyncs on the next run. The jar is a binary on the build path (INV-7), so the
# gate asserts its SHA-256 against the value Gradle publishes for this version —
# see the `gradle wrapper jar` lane in tools/gate.sh.
/.gradle
/captures/
/local.properties
GeneratedPluginRegistrant.java
.cxx/

# Remember to never publicly share your keystore.
# See https://flutter.dev/to/reference-keystore
key.properties
**/*.keystore
**/*.jks
